  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The architecture doc covers: the /mcp/{area} route and area model; A10 auth flow and refusals; the decision capability, lookup search and result mapper; the five tools with visibility and hints; the widget and its embedding; kill switch, rate and size limits; telemetry; and links to ADR-028 A10, ADR-013, ADR-015, ADR-032 — each claim tied to a real file path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The how-to guide gives the steps to add a tool to an existing area and to add a new area (new /mcp/{area}, not a second MCP server), including the tests each needs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every path named exists (doc-drift-audit clean); the only edit to M365-COPILOT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md is replacing the retired 'Spaarke Copilot' term at L33.</constraint>
  </constraints>

